Report Guix System update state in upgrades-installed-check.

upgrades-installed-check walks a chain of per-distribution branches to decide
whether updates are available.  Add a Guix System branch (detected by
/run/current-system) before the Archlinux branch.

The Guix helper resolves /etc/guix/channels.scm through Guix's own restricted
channel evaluator and authenticated channel checkout code.  It compares those
resolved revisions with /etc/qubes-applied-guix-channels.scm, which is generated
as part of the active system generation.  This checks the actual channel set,
honors explicit commit pins, includes the Qubes channel, and keeps reporting an
update until a successful system reconfiguration switches to a generation made
from the new revisions.  A successful full check caches its authenticated
result so the standard post-update skip-refresh hook can verify the applied
generation without network access.

Like the existing apt/dnf branches, a refresh or authentication failure emits
no true/false result and returns nonzero.  upgrades-status-notify therefore
leaves dom0's previous state unchanged instead of incorrectly clearing the
notification during a network failure.

Upstream: QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux,
package-managers/upgrades-installed-check.
Status: should-upstream (adds a new distro branch alongside the existing
debian/arch/gentoo/alpine branches; other distributions are unaffected).

diff --git a/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check b/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check
index ceb3be2..63f7c22 100755
--- a/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check
+++ b/package-managers/upgrades-installed-check
@@ -46,6 +46,31 @@ elif [ -e /etc/debian_version ]; then
     # shellcheck disable=SC2266
     echo "$apt_get_upgrade_output" | awk "/^Inst/{ print $2 }" | [ "$(wc -L)" -eq 0 ] && echo "true" || echo "false"
     echo "$apt_get_upgrade_output" >&2
+elif [ -e /run/current-system ]; then
+    ## Guix System
+    guix_bin="$(command -v guix || echo /run/current-system/profile/bin/guix)"
+    checker=/usr/lib/qubes/guix-updates-installed-check.scm
+    state=/etc/qubes-applied-guix-channels.scm
+    channels=/etc/guix/channels.scm
+    cache=/var/lib/qubes/guix-update-check-latest.scm
+
+    if [ ! -x "$guix_bin" ]; then
+        echo "Guix update check: guix command is unavailable" >&2
+        exit_code=1
+    elif [ ! -r "$checker" ] || [ ! -r "$state" ] || [ ! -r "$channels" ]; then
+        echo "Guix update check: required checker input is unavailable" >&2
+        exit_code=1
+    elif $skip_refresh; then
+        "$guix_bin" repl -q -- "$checker" "$state" "$channels" "$cache" \
+            skip-refresh
+        exit_code="$?"
+    else
+        # `guix repl` supplies the same Guix modules as the running command.
+        # The helper uses authenticated channel resolution rather than parsing
+        # unauthenticated `git ls-remote` output.
+        "$guix_bin" repl -q -- "$checker" "$state" "$channels" "$cache"
+        exit_code="$?"
+    fi
 elif [ -e /etc/arch-release ]; then
     ## Archlinux
     checkupdates >/dev/null 2>&1
